Package: seagate-nas2bay-boot
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: armhf
Maintainer: laserbirdx <https://github.com/laserbirdx>
Depends: initramfs-tools, mdadm, lvm2, u-boot-tools, device-tree-compiler, e2fsprogs, util-linux
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/laserbirdx/seagate-nas2bay-omv
Description: Boot support for Debian 12 on the Seagate NAS 2-Bay (n090201 / SRPD20)
 Lets the stock Seagate U-Boot start Debian 12 from a loop-mounted root image
 on the existing RAID1+LVM data volume, without touching NAND:
  - fixed Armada 370 device tree (SATA clocks, USB 3.0 PCIe, all 6 LEDs)
  - uImage builder (zImage + initramfs in one image) and kernel hook
  - custom initramfs /init with two-stage fail-safe rollback to the factory OS
  - nas-boot-select tool to switch between Debian and the factory OS
  - first-boot setup and boot health check
